msgid "Shotwell"
msgstr "Shotwell"

#: misc/shotwell.appdata.xml.in:9
msgid "Popular photo manager"
msgstr "Gewilde foto bestuurder"

#: data/org.gnome.Shotwell.appdata.xml.in:11
msgid ""
"Shotwell is an easy-to-use, fast photo organizer designed for the GNOME "
"desktop. It allows you to import photos from your camera or disk, organize "
"them by date and subject matter, even ratings. It also offers basic photo "
"editing, like crop, red-eye correction, color adjustments, and straighten. "
"Shotwell’s non-destructive photo editor does not alter your master photos, "
"making it easy to experiment and correct errors."
msgstr ""
"Shotwell is 'n maklike, vinnige foto-organiseerder wat ontwerp is vir die "
"GNOME-tafelblad. Dit stel u in staat om foto's vanaf u kamera of skyf in te "
"voer, dit volgens datum en onderwerp te organiseer, selfs graderings. Dit "
"bied ook basiese fotoredigering, soos gewas, korreksie van rooi oë, "
"kleuraanpassings en reguit. Die nie-vernietigende fotoredigeerder van "
"Shotwell verander nie u meesterfoto's nie, wat dit maklik maak om te "
"eksperimenteer en foute reg te stel."

#: misc/shotwell.appdata.xml.in:18
msgid ""
"When ready, Shotwell can upload your photos to various web sites, such as "
"Facebook, Flickr, Google Photos, and more."
msgstr ""
"As u gereed is, kan Shotwell u foto's na verskillende webwerwe, soos "
"Facebook, Flickr, Google Photos en meer, oplaai."

#: data/org.gnome.Shotwell.appdata.xml.in:22
msgid "Shotwell supports JPEG, PNG, TIFF, and a variety of RAW file formats."
msgstr ""
"Shotwell ondersteun JPEG, PNG, TIFF en 'n verskeidenheid RAW-lêerformate."

#: data/org.gnome.Shotwell.appdata.xml.in:53
msgid "The Shotwell developers"
msgstr "Die Shotwell ontwikkelaars"

